@startuml 06_physics_contact_and_jump
title Gameplay Example — landing on a platform enables jumping

autonumber

actor Player
participant "input.Adapter" as InputAdapter
participant "event.Bus" as Bus
participant "Scene\n(WorldScene)" as Scene
participant "script.Engine\n(Python VM)" as VM
participant "player_controller.py" as PlayerScript
participant "PhysicsSystem" as Physics

== The jump request is latched, but only honored if already grounded ==

Player -> InputAdapter : presses Space (bound to action "jump")
InputAdapter -> Bus : Emit(ScriptEmitted{Name: "JumpRequested"})
Bus -> Scene : ScriptEmitted handler
Scene -> VM : CallOnEvent("JumpRequested", nil)
VM -> PlayerScript : on_event("JumpRequested", payload)
alt is_grounded
  PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : pending_jump = True
else airborne
  PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : ignored -- not queued for landing\n(queuing was tried and reverted: it caused\nan unrequested jump the moment the player landed)
end

== Meanwhile, physics detects the player landing ==

Scene -> Physics : Step(dt)
Physics -> Physics : box2d.World.Step(dt)\n// player's dynamic body contacts\n// a static platform body
Physics -> Bus : Emit(BeginContact{"player", "platform_2"})
Bus -> Scene : handler
Scene -> VM : CallOnEvent("BeginContact", {A: "player", B: "platform_2"})
VM -> PlayerScript : on_event("BeginContact", payload)
PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : _touching["platform_2"] = True\nis_grounded = True
note right
  is_grounded is derived from a {name: touching?} dict over
  GROUND_OBJECTS, not a bool or counter -- the player can touch
  more than one ground object at once (e.g. brushing a crate
  while standing on the ground), and a bool/counter both had
  reproducible bugs where jumping silently stopped working.
  See the script's own module docstring for the full reasoning.
end note

== Next updateScripts(dt): the jump actually happens ==

Scene -> VM : CallScriptUpdate("player_controller.py", "update", playerGO, dt)
VM -> PlayerScript : update(dt)
alt pending_jump and is_grounded
  PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : self.apply_linear_impulse_to_center(0, -JUMP_IMPULSE)
  PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : self.reset_animation("jump")\npending_jump = False
else
  PlayerScript -> PlayerScript : nothing to do this frame
end

note over Physics, PlayerScript
  Later, when the player leaves the platform, PhysicsSystem emits
  EndContact the same way, and on_event flips
  _touching["platform_2"] = False, re-deriving is_grounded from
  whatever ground objects (if any) are still touched.
end note

@enduml
